{
  "title": "Potassium\u2013glucose coupling does not establish improved fasting insulin prediction across two NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "We tested a centered potassium\u00d7log glucose interaction beyond flexible component effects and conventional demographic,adiposity and renal measures. Source NHANES2015\u201316 included 1912 fasting adults;the separately sampled2017\u201318 target included 1863. Target weighted log-insulin MSE was 0.288942 versus 0.289441;gain -0.000499,500 joint stratified-PSU-bootstrap95% interval [-0.005966,0.002057]. Source fivefoldCV gain was -0.003946. The feature did not establish improved prediction. This negative cross-sectional test is not equivalence or evidence against potassium-related insulin physiology. Independent-sample transfer was tested within NHANES;there was no independent health-system validation. AI-authored and author-self-checked.",
